orkspace/... (57 more)\n\nWrite the corresponding R code to implement the following task ($filename-Part4-dry-experiment-3-saved$):\n\n{\n    \"task_id\": \"Part 4-dry-experiment-3\",\n    \"task_description\": \"Prepare a discussion document outlining potential therapeutic targets revealed through GO and KEGG analyses, focusing on the implications for liposarcoma treatment strategies.\",\n    \"input\": \"Results from the GO and KEGG analyses, including enriched biological processes, pathways, and references to datasets GSE202361 and GSE205492. The input should also include literature references that discuss specific genes implicated in liposarcoma treatment.\",\n    \"output\": \"A comprehensive discussion document summarizing key therapeutic targets, their implications for treatment strategies, and expected outcomes. The document should present findings in a written format, highlighting specific genes and pathways of interest.\"\n}.\n\nGlobal plan generated by gpt-5.2-thinking (must follow unless conflicting with user feedback):\n## Execution Order\n\n**0. Repo bootstrap (shared across all parts)**\n1. Create standard folder tree and config files.\n2. Write a single **dataset manifest** (what to fetch, where from, and expected outputs).\n3. Add lightweight “driver” scripts that call each step and stop if contracts are not met.\n\n**1. Cohort discovery & eligibility (Part 1)**\n1. **P1-1** Systematic search (TCGA/GTEx/local biobanks) → raw search tables.\n2. **P1-2** TCGA “Liposarcoma” case query → tcga case table.\n3. **P1-3** GTEx “sarcoma” tissue filter → gtex sample table.\n4. **P1-4** Local biobank unique IDs + dedup mapping → local id table + dedup keys.\n5. **P1-5** Apply inclusion/exclusion → final eligible cohort table.\n6. **P1-6** Record structured characteristics → sample metadata master table.\n7. **P1-7** Summary stats → summary report tables/figures.\n8. **P1-8** Meeting packet generation (agenda + cohort summary) → meeting PDF/MD.\n\n**2. Data acquisition + preprocessing (Part 2)**\n1. **P2-1** Download TCGA + GEO (GSE202361) per manifest → raw data in `data/raw/`.\n2. **P2-2** QC on downloaded data → QC metrics tables + plots.\n3. **P2-3** Normalization:\n   - DESeq2 normalization for count matrices (RNA-seq).\n   - gcRMA for microarray CELs **only if CEL files exist**; otherwise skip with note.\n4. **P2-4** Auto-log preprocessing steps → one reproducibility report with versions + parameters.\n\n**3. Differential expression (Part 3)**\n1. **P3-1** Load normalized matrices + metadata (TCGA + GSE202361).\n2. **P3-2** Build design matrix (limma) and contrasts.\n3. **P3-3** Fit model (lmFit).\n4. **P3-4** eBayes.\n5. **P3-5** topTable export (DEGs + full ranked list) + volcano/MA plots.\n\n**4. Functional enrichment + interpretation (Part 4)**\n1. **P4-1** GO enrichment on significant DEGs (GSE202361 focus) → GO results tables/plots.\n2. **P4-2** KEGG enrichment → KEGG results tables/plots.\n3. **P4-3** Discussion document: candidate targets + pathways + citations → MD/PDF.\n\n**5. lncRNA immune checkpoint + survival/prediction (Part 5)**\n1. **P5-1** Acquire TCGA RNA-seq with lncRNAs + immune checkpoint genes list → lncRNA matrix + mapping table.\n2. **P5-2** Expression analysis (association with checkpoints, group comparisons) → stats tables/plots.\n3. **P5-3** Kaplan–Meier survival on high/low lncRNA expression → KM plots + HR tables.\n4. **P5-4** Predictive modeling for immunotherapy response:\n   - If response labels absent, run as “proxy modeling” (e.g., checkpoint expression / TMB if available) and **clearly label**.\n5. **P5-5** Challenges log → append-only issue log.\n\n---\n\n## File Contract\n\n### Global conventions\n- **Root dirs**\n  - `config/` (YAML/JSON configs, manifests)\n  - `data/raw/` (downloaded/unmodified)\n  - `data/interim/` (normalized, filtered, merged)\n  - `results/` (final tables/plots)\n  - `reports/` (markdown/html/pdf)\n  - `logs/` (runtime logs, session info)\n  - `scripts/` (R scripts)\n- **Naming**\n  - Dataset key: `TCGA_LPS`, `GTEx_SARC`, `GSE202361`, `LOCAL_BIOBANK`\n  - Step key: `P1_.. P5_..` (e.g., `P3_DE_limma`)\n  - Timestamp optional: `YYYYMMDD` for manual reruns; automated runs overwrite “latest” symlinks if desired.\n- **Tables**: `.tsv` (preferred) or `.csv` with explicit delimiter noted in header.\n- **R objects**: `.rds` with `saveRDS()` for portability.\n- **Plots**: `.png` for quick view + `.pdf` for publication.\n\n### Required core files (produced once and reused)\n1. `config/project_config.yml`\n   - paths, organism (hg38), gene id type preference (Ensembl), cutoffs (FDR, logFC).\n2. `config/dataset_manifest.tsv`\n   - columns: `dataset_id, source, accession, data_type, url_or_api, expected_files, notes`.\n3. `data/interim/sample_metadata_master.tsv`\n   - columns (minimum): `sample_id, cohort, source, platform, tissue, diagnosis, subtype, sex, age, grade, batch, group, inclusion_flag, exclusion_reason`.\n4. `data/interim/expression_counts_<dataset_id>.rds` (if RNA-seq counts)\n   - matrix-like object: genes x samples; rownames=gene IDs; colnames=sample IDs.\n5. `data/interim/expression_norm_<method>_<dataset_id>.rds`\n   - e.g., `expression_norm_deseq2_TCGA_LPS.rds`, `expression_norm_gcrma_GSE202361.rds` (only if microarray CELs).\n\n### Per-step outputs (minimum contract)\n- **P1**\n  - `results/P1/search_tcga_cases.tsv`\n  - `results/P1/search_gtex_samples.tsv`\n  - `results/P1/search_local_biobank.tsv`\n  - `data/interim/dedup_sample_keys.tsv` (columns: `source, original_id, canonical_id`)\n  - `data/interim/eligible_samples.tsv`\n  - `results/P1/summary_stats.tsv` + `results/P1/summary_plots.pdf`\n  - `reports/P1/meeting_packet.md` (or `.pdf`)\n- **P2**\n  - `logs/P2/download_log.tsv` (file, status, checksum/size)\n  - `results/P2/qc_metrics_<dataset_id>.tsv`\n  - `results/P2/qc_plots_<dataset_id>.pdf`\n  - `reports/P2/preprocessing_report.md` (includes `sessionInfo()`)\n- **P3**\n  - `data/interim/design_matrix_<dataset_id>.tsv`\n  - `data/interim/fit_limma_<dataset_id>.rds`\n  - `results/P3/deg_topTable_<dataset_id>.tsv` (significant)\n  - `results/P3/ranked_genes_<dataset_id>.tsv` (full)\n  - `results/P3/volcano_<dataset_id>.pdf`, `results/P3/ma_<dataset_id>.pdf`\n- **P4**\n  - `results/P4/go_enrichment_GSE202361.tsv` + `go_dotplot.pdf`\n  - `results/P4/kegg_enrichment_GSE202361.tsv` + `kegg_dotplot.pdf`\n  - `reports/P4/targets_discussion.md` (and optional `.pdf`)\n- **P5**\n  - `data/interim/lncrna_checkpoint_matrix_TCGA_LPS.rds`\n  - `results/P5/lncrna_checkpoint_associations.tsv`\n  - `results/P5/km_results.tsv` + `km_plots.pdf`\n  - `results/P5/predictive_models.tsv` (model specs + metrics)\n  - `reports/P5/challenges_log.md` (append-only)\n\n---\n\n## Error Prevention Rules\n\n### Paths & reproducibility\n- Use **relative paths** from project root; scripts must accept `--config config/project_config.yml`.\n- Every script begins with:\n  - `set.seed(1)`\n  - `options(stringsAsFactors=FALSE)`\n  - write `logs/<step>_sessionInfo.txt` from `sessionInfo()`.\n\n### Missing files / partial downloads\n- Download step writes `download_log.tsv` with `status={ok,missing,failed}` and file sizes.\n- If expected raw data missing:\n  - For GEO: fallback to `GEOquery::getGEO()` for series matrix when raw not accessible.\n  - For TCGA: if GDC API unavailable, allow **manual drop-in** to `data/raw/TCGA_LPS/` and proceed.\n- Never silently proceed with empty matrices; require `nrow>0` and `ncol>1`.\n\n### Package issues (minimal installs)\nContainer already has key packages for Parts 2–3 (DESeq2/limma/edgeR/GEOquery/affy/gcrma).\nAdditional packages likely needed:\n- **Enrichment (Part 4)**: `clusterProfiler`, `org.Hs.eg.db`, `enrichplot`, `DOSE`  \n  Minimal install (BiocManager; run once in bootstrap script):\n  ```r\n  if (!requireNamespace(\"BiocManager\", quietly=TRUE)) install.packages(\"BiocManager\")\n  BiocManager::install(c(\"clusterProfiler\",\"org.Hs.eg.db\",\"enrichplot\",\"DOSE\"), update=FALSE, ask=FALSE)\n  ```\n- **Survival plots/models (Part 5)**: `survival`, `survminer` (often present, but not guaranteed)\n  ```r\n  install.packages(c(\"survival\",\"survminer\"))\n  ```\nFallback if install fails/timeouts: produce survival tables/curves using base `survival` only (no `survminer`), output CSV + basic PDF.\n\n### ID mismatches / annotation pitfalls\n- Enforce a single gene ID type per matrix (prefer **Ensembl**). Store mapping:\n  - `data/interim/gene_id_map.tsv` (ensembl, entrez, symbol).\n- If mixed IDs detected, stop and request remap; do not merge on symbols without version-stripping rules.\n- For KEGG/GO requiring Entrez: convert via `clusterProfiler::bitr()` with explicit `drop=TRUE` and report conversion rate; if <70% mapped, warn and output both mapped/unmapped lists.\n\n### Timeouts / resource limits\n- Split tasks into independent scripts per step (`scripts/P2_download.R`, `scripts/P3_limma.R`, etc.).\n- Cache intermediate `.rds` objects; downstream scripts never recompute upstream steps if `.rds` exists and passes validation.\n- For large TCGA downloads, support “counts-only mode”:\n  - prefer GDC “HTSeq - Counts” summarized matrices over BAM/FASTQ.\n- For QC, if FASTQ unavailable, run QC on count distributions/library sizes instead and label as “post-alignment QC”.\n\n### Data integrity checks\n- Always validate:\n  - sample IDs in expression matrix exactly match `sample_metadata_master.tsv` after canonicalization.\n  - no duplicated `canonical_id` within a dataset unless technical replicates are explicitly labeled.\n- Write a `results/<step>/warnings.tsv` if non-fatal issues occur.\n\n---\n\n## Minimal Validation Checklist\n\n1. **Bootstrap**\n   - Folder tree exists; `config/project_config.yml` and `config/dataset_manifest.tsv` readable.\n2. **Cohort tables**\n   - `eligible_samples.tsv` exists; `inclusion_flag` present; no duplicated `canonical_id`.\n3. **Raw data presence**\n   - `logs/P2/download_log.tsv` has all manifest entries marked `ok` or explicitly justified `missing`.\n4. **Expression matrices**\n   - Counts/norm `.rds` load; dimensions reasonable (`ncol>=2`, `nrow>=1000` for RNA-seq).\n   - Column names match metadata sample IDs (100% overlap after canonicalization).\n5. **DE outputs**\n   - `deg_topTable_<dataset>.tsv` has required columns (`logFC`, `adj.P.Val`/`FDR`, `P.Value`).\n6. **Enrichment outputs**\n   - GO/KEGG result tables non-empty or contain explicit “no terms passed cutoff” note + used thresholds.\n7. **Survival/prediction**\n   - Survival table has `time`, `event` fields; KM plots generated or base fallback used.\n8. **Reproducibility**\n   - Each step produced `*_sessionInfo.txt` and scripts wrote parameter headers into reports.\n",
