                    "content": "The HISTORY of your other task executions is as follows:\nPart 1 1: Provided R code to compile a proxy sample list from the allowed local GEO files with graceful missing-file handling and save it under /workspace/coding3; the run succeeded and produced /workspace/coding3/sample_list_final.csv with 276 records.\nPart 1 2: Generated the liposarcoma cases dataset from allowlisted local files with graceful handling and saved it to /workspace/coding3/tcga_liposarcoma_cases.csv.\nPart 1 3: The GTEx sarcoma-filtering R script ran successfully and saved the output to /workspace/coding3/gtex_sarcoma_sample_metadata.csv.\nPart 1 4: Unique sample IDs were extracted from the three allowlisted biobank-related files, standardized into a shared schema with placeholders where metadata was missing, deduplicated to 168 unique samples, and saved to /workspace/coding3/biobank_unique_sample_ids.csv.\nPart 1 5: The task history shows successful generation of sample lists and metadata from prior steps, and the current step produced `/workspace/coding3/eligible_samples_final.csv` by applying inclusion/exclusion criteria to the three allowlisted GEO inputs.\nPart 1 6: The task created a structured sample characteristics file at /workspace/coding3/sample_characteristics_detailed.csv, with warnings from grepl() due to multiple patterns; these can be eliminated by collapsing patterns with paste(..., collapse=\"|\") if a rerun is desired.\nPart 1 7: Summary statistics for samples were successfully computed from allowlisted inputs and saved to /workspace/coding3/sample_statistics_summary.csv.\nPart 1 8: Previously ran the meeting-notes script, which successfully saved `/workspace/coding3/meeting_notes_part1_dry_experiment_8.txt`, with repeated confirmations and offers to provide a structured CSV/JSON summary.\nPart 2 1: The task ran successfully, staging available allowlisted GEO files and creating placeholders for missing datasets, with outputs saved to `/workspace/coding3/part2_downloads/`, a manifest at `/workspace/coding3/part2_download_manifest.csv`, and a log at `/workspace/coding3/part2_download_log.txt`.\nPart 2 2: QC completed successfully with outputs saved under `/workspace/coding3`: `qc_report.txt`, `qc_metrics.csv`, `qc_excluded_samples.csv`, `rna_degradation_plot.png`, and `qc_sample_sources_combined.csv`, confirming pass/fail assessment and sample traceability.\nPart 2 3: All requested steps completed successfully, including corrected Part 2-dry-experiment-3 code generation and execution with exit code 0, followed by final confirmation outputs.\nPart 2 4: All tasks completed and outputs were saved under /workspace/coding3, including the preprocessing documentation markdown at /workspace/coding3/preprocessing_steps_documentation.md, with prior steps producing staged download manifests/logs and QC reports/metrics.\nPart 3 1: Part 3-dry-experiment-1 was corrected and executed successfully (exit code 0), loading GSE202361 TPM/counts plus TCGA liposarcoma cases into analysis-ready R objects, avoiding the prior tximport issue and placeholder failure, and writing all concrete outputs under `/workspace/coding3` (`gse202361_tpm_loaded.csv`, `gse202361_counts_loaded.csv`, `tcga_liposarcoma_cases_loaded.csv`, `rnaseq_loaded_objects.rds`, `part3_dry_experiment_1_object_summary.csv`, and `part3_dry_experiment_1_load_log.txt`).\nPart 3 2: Design matrix creation for Part 3‑dry‑experiment‑2 succeeded; outputs saved to `/workspace/coding3/design_matrix.csv`, `/workspace/coding3/design_matrix.rds`, and `/workspace/coding3/design_matrix_log.txt`, with optional next steps to preview or proceed to lmFit.\nPart 3 3: Part 3‑dry‑experiment‑3 (limma::lmFit) ran successfully, saving the fitted model, coefficients/SE CSV, and log under /workspace/coding3, and I offered to proceed with the next eBayes step.\nPart 3 4: Part 3 completed through eBayes with a successful fallback path: when no direct `lmFit` RDS was found, the model was rebuilt from `/workspace/coding3/gse202361_counts_loaded.csv` and `/workspace/coding3/design_matrix.rds`, `limma::eBayes` ran successfully, and a full `topTable` (57,773 rows) plus summary/log/object outputs were written to `/workspace/coding3` (`part3_dry_experiment_4_ebayes_fit.rds`, `part3_dry_experiment_4_topTable_all.csv`, `part3_dry_experiment_4_ebayes_summary.csv`, `part3_dry_experiment_4_ebayes_log.txt`); the only warning was limma’s non-fatal zero-variance offset message.\nPart 3 5: The conversation shows a sequence of dry-experiment tasks completed successfully across Parts 1–3, culminating in Part 3-dry-experiment-5 where R code was provided to run limma::topTable with filtering criteria, but due to the strict allowlist excluding the eBayes RDS path, the script would generate a placeholder DEGs file and log a warning, and the user confirmed execution succeeded.\nPart 4 1: Completion confirmed with exit code 0; GO enrichment ran under allowlist constraints, produced a placeholder results table due to no eligible DEG input, and wrote `/workspace/coding3/go_enrichment_results.csv` plus `/workspace/coding3/part4_dry_experiment_1_log.txt`.\nPart 4 2: {\n    \"task_id\": \"Part 4-dry-experiment-2\",\n    \"task_description\": \"Perform Kyoto Encyclopedia of Genes and Genomes (KEGG) pathway analysis on the significant DEGs to identify relevant biological pathways.\",\n    \"input\": \"The same data frame used for the GO analysis, containing significant DEGs with an adjusted P-value < 0.05. This input should include gene identifiers and expression values, formatted for KEGG analysis.\",\n    \"output\": \"A tab-delimited file that includes pathway names, associated gene counts, and adjusted P-values for the KEGG analysis, structured in a tabular format with columns for pathway name, gene count, and adjusted P-value.\"\n}\nTask failed after escalation chain: Part 4-dry-experiment-2\n1) 5.2-codex execute failed\n2) 5.3-codex execute failed\nFinal diagnostic:\nexitcode: 0 (execution succeeded)\nCode output: Part 4-dry-experiment-2 started at: 2026-04-01 07:17:39.516062 \n[2026-04-01 07:17:39] Using DEG candidate input: /workspace/coding3/go_enrichment_results.csv \n[2026-04-01 07:17:39] No usable DEG table found; deriving proxy significant genes from GSE202361 TPM by high variance. \n[2026-04-01 07:17:41] Gene set size for KEGG: 2889 \n[2026-04-01 07:17:41] Warning: clusterProfiler/org.Hs.eg.db unavailable; writing non-empty fallback summary from input genes. \n[2026-04-01 07:17:41] KEGG results saved: /workspace/coding3/kegg_analysis_results.tsv \n[2026-04-01 07:17:41] Rows written: 1 \nPart 4-dry-experiment-2 completed at: 2026-04-01 07:17:41.329983\nquality_guard_failed_markers=['fallback']\nPart 4 2: KEGG analysis completed successfully after installing clusterProfiler/org.Hs.eg.db and dependencies; results written to `/workspace/coding3/kegg_analysis_results.tsv` with significant pathways shown, then top‑20 pathways were exported and a bar plot generated at `/workspace/coding3/kegg_top20_pathways.tsv` and `/workspace/coding3/kegg_top20_barplot.png`, with minor non‑fatal gene ID mapping warnings.\nPart 4 3: Summary of the conversation: Part 4‑dry‑experiment‑3 was implemented with R code that used only allowlisted inputs (GSE202361 TPM), handled missing GO/KEGG and GSE205492 inputs with placeholders, and wrote the discussion document and log to `/workspace/coding3/part4_dry_experiment_3_discussion.md` and `/workspace/coding3/part4_dry_experiment_3_log.txt`; execution succeeded and outputs were confirmed.\nPart 5 1: The work across Parts 1–4 successfully produced cohort/sample lists, QC and preprocessing outputs, limma DE results, and GO/KEGG enrichment (with initial placeholder/fallback handling and later completed KEGG results), then Part 5‑dry‑experiment‑1 ran successfully with exit code 0 and generated proxy lncRNA/immune checkpoint expression and clinical-attributes outputs under `/workspace/coding3`.\nPart 5 2: Part 5‑dry‑experiment‑2 completed successfully: DESeq2 ran, outputs and plots were written under `/workspace/coding3`, and the warnings reflect expected cases—an empty correlation matrix due to no overlapping significant lncRNAs/checkpoint genes in TPM and many `padj` NAs removed from the volcano plot.\nPart 5 3: Part 5‑dry‑experiment‑3 ran successfully (exit code 0) with no console output, generating KM survival results and plots plus logs under /workspace/coding3, and the next step offered to preview or inspect the outputs.\n\nConstraints:\n1) Use only existing files under /workspace listed below; do not invent names like summary_statistics_report.csv.\n2) Prefer graceful handling for missing files: print warning and create placeholder output instead of hard stop.\n3) For missing files/packages, do not use exit(), quit(status=1), or stop(...); continue with placeholder outputs.\n4) Save outputs under /workspace/coding3 with concrete filenames.\n5) Do not write final outputs to /workspace root.\n6) Use ONLY the selected files below as inputs for this task.\n7) DO NOT scan/probe whole directories (forbidden: list.files('/workspace', recursive=TRUE), Sys.glob('/workspace/**')).\n8) If combining multiple tables, first map them to a shared schema and then merge with data.table::rbindlist(fill=TRUE).\n\nContainer environment (for package decision):\nDocker image: rocker/verse\nR package probe status: ok\nInstalled key packages: DESeq2, limma, edgeR, GEOquery, affy, gcrma, jsonlite, readxl, data.table, httr, curl\nMissing key packages: (none)\n\nPackage policy:\n- Prefer already installed packages.\n- If missing packages are required by this task, decide whether to install minimal extras in-code.\n- Avoid broad/full installs; install only what's needed for this task.\n\nDataset selection for this task (strict input allowlist):\n- /workspace/data/GSE202361_AllSamples_TPM.txt.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE247026_Sample_genes_fpkm.xlsx\n- /workspace/data/GSE202361_AllSamples_rawcount.txt.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE168205_annotated_combined.counts.txt.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE213065_Sarcoma_ecotyper_tpm_bulksamples.txt.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE91061_BMS038109Sample.hg19KnownGene.rld.csv.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE91061_BMS038109Sample.hg19KnownGene.fpkm.csv.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE230773_Read_counts.xlsx\n\nAvailable files:\n- /workspace/coding3.log\n- /workspace/coding3/biobank_unique_sample_ids.csv\n- /workspace/coding3/deseq2_normalized_counts.csv\n- /workspace/coding3/design_matrix.csv\n- /workspace/coding3/design_matrix.rds\n- /workspace/coding3/design_matrix_log.txt\n- /workspace/coding3/ebayes_fit.rds\n- /workspace/coding3/ebayes_log.txt\n- /workspace/coding3/ebayes_statistics.csv\n- /workspace/coding3/eligible_samples_final.csv\n- /workspace/coding3/gcrma_normalized_expression.txt\n- /workspace/coding3/go_enrichment_results.csv\n- /workspace/coding3/gse202361_counts_loaded.csv\n- /workspace/coding3/gse202361_tpm_loaded.csv\n- /workspace/coding3/gtex_sarcoma_sample_metadata.csv\n- /workspace/coding3/kegg_analysis_results.tsv\n- /workspace/coding3/limma_lmfit_coefficients_se.csv\n- /workspace/coding3/limma_lmfit_object.rds\n- /workspace/coding3/meeting_notes_part1_dry_experiment_8.txt\n- /workspace/coding3/part2_download_log.txt\n- /workspace/coding3/part2_download_manifest.csv\n- /workspace/coding3/part2_downloads/GSE161616_MISSING.txt\n- /workspace/coding3/part2_downloads/GSE191132_MISSING.txt\n- /workspace/coding3/part2_downloads/GSE202361_AllSamples_TPM.txt.gz\n- /workspace/coding3/part2_downloads/GSE202361_AllSamples_rawcount.txt.gz\n- /workspace/coding3/part2_downloads/GSE205492_MISSING.txt\n- /workspace/coding3/part2_downloads/GSE213065_Sarcoma_ecotyper_tpm_bulksamples.txt.gz\n- /workspace/coding3/part2_downloads/GSE230773_Read_counts.xlsx\n- /workspace/coding3/part2_downloads/GSE243759_MISSING.txt\n- /workspace/coding3/part2_downloads/GSE243904_DGE_NORM_IB11_PRMT5_Treated_vs_notreated_LIMMA_T-TEST_AFFYX.txt.gz\n- /workspace/coding3/part2_do