n- /workspace/coding3/tmp_code_3a6203bd7f81014a399c8b12fabc5b4d.r\n- /workspace/coding3/tmp_code_3e943d9b907a3edd978d470e5396e7c1.r\n- /workspace/coding3/tmp_code_3e9a8655ac7f8a6de547c81d9a25c29b.r\n- /workspace/coding3/tmp_code_4128207953c7204a63030dd83da03c60.r\n- /workspace/coding3/tmp_code_4479307bdcdced313fdfc4cb90e51e1f.r\n- /workspace/coding3/tmp_code_4cc8f7c298aae090748c3cb7049e30ee.r\n- /workspace/coding3/tmp_code_62e08f2607ecbc8b64e99861e4553c1f.r\n- /workspace/coding3/tmp_code_67f5f1bca1ccc755d2720f464421b0c7.r\n- /workspace/coding3/tmp_code_69c971a32b612e24ab17130fb951baec.r\n- /workspace/coding3/tmp_code_6edb49549ccbb5b9815ca59bdfe0d3f9.r\n- /workspace/coding3/tmp_code_83c8914e25fe05f9be99bea93244d32a.r\n- /workspace/coding3/tmp_code_869dfb35fb44745e4b38ca13899b398c.r\n- /workspace/coding3/tmp_code_9cdf2a4da5d0c537a70945cb75f6a526.r\n- /workspace/coding3/tmp_code_b42444644a3aff94b78be3aa1b530c9d.r\n- /workspace/coding3/tmp_code_bccb70cc6c7a0f7bfa5928ab2f68b381.r\n- /workspace/coding3/tmp_code_c33bbd79857ce2fadc8fea29464ce2a2.r\n- /workspace/coding3/tmp_code_d2098aafcd987d34815247a465d3efc3.r\n- /workspace/coding3/tmp_code_e1058e67ea5cea01d1f8a22b1ab92442.r\n- /workspace/coding3/tmp_code_fc6e1b453db8d3a6638ce76096ad9729.r\n- /workspace/coding3/tmp_code_fe4e83c20cf16363808c767a01449a72.r\n- /workspace/data/GSE152737_RAW.tar\n- /workspace/data/GSE152778_CAMTA1_FLAG_peaks.narrowPeak.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE152778_EV_IgG_peaks.narrowPeak.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE152778_TAZ4SA_FLAG_peaks.narrowPeak.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE152778_TC_FLAG_peaks.narrowPeak.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE152778_TFE3_chip_peaks.narrowPeak.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE152778_YAP5SA_chip_peaks.narrowPeak.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE152778_YT_chip_peaks.narrowPeak.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE161616_RAW.tar\n- /workspace/data/GSE168205_RAW.tar\n- /workspace/data/GSE168205_annotated_combined.counts.txt.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE191132_RAW.tar\n- /workspace/data/GSE202361_AllSamples_TPM.txt.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE202361_AllSamples_rawcount.txt.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE205492_rnaseq_workshop_normalized_counts.txt.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE213065_Sarcoma_ecotyper_tpm_bulksamples.txt.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE230773_Read_counts.xlsx\n- /workspace/data/GSE241225_RAW.tar\n- /workspace/data/GSE241225_vc8817.rda.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE243759_RAW.tar\n- /workspace/data/GSE243904_DGE_NORM_IB11_PRMT5_Treated_vs_notreated_LIMMA_T-TEST_AFFYX.txt.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE247026_Sample_genes_fpkm.xlsx\n- /workspace/data/GSE267611_IC90_48h_1765-92vsDMSO_48h_1765-92.complete.txt.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE267611_IC90_48h_402-91vsDMSO_48h_402-91.complete.txt.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE267611_IC90_48h_A673vsDMSO_48h_A673.complete.txt.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE267611_IC90_48h_BERvsDMSO_48h_BER.complete.txt.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE267611_IC90_48h_DL221vsDMSO_48h_DL221.complete.txt.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE267611_IC90_48h_DTC1vsDMSO_48h_DTC1.complete.txt.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE267611_IC90_48h_JNDSRCTvsDMSO_48h_JNDSRCT.complete.txt.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE267611_IC90_48h_SUCCS1vsDMSO_48h_SUCCS1.complete.txt.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE267611_IC90_48h_TTC466vsDMSO_48h_TTC466.complete.txt.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE267611_iERG562vsiERG197.complete.txt.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE267611_sample_meta_out.txt.gz\n- /workspace/data/GSE55465_RAW.tar\n- /workspace/... (57 more)\n\nWrite the corresponding R code to implement the following task ($filename-Part5-dry-experiment-4-saved$):\n\n{\n    \"task_id\": \"Part 5-dry-experiment-4\",\n    \"task_description\": \"Investigate the predictive value of lncRNAs for response to immunotherapy through statistical modeling.\",\n    \"input\": \"Expression levels of significant lncRNAs (continuous) and clinical outcome data regarding immunotherapy response (binary outcome: responder vs. non-responder).\",\n    \"output\": \"Statistical models (e.g., logistic regression) indicating the predictive value of lncRNAs as biomarkers for immunotherapy response, along with associated statistical metrics (odds ratios, confidence intervals).\"\n}.\n\nGlobal plan generated by gpt-5.2-thinking (must follow unless conflicting with user feedback):\n## Execution Order\n\n**0. Repo bootstrap (shared across all parts)**\n1. Create standard folder tree and config files.\n2. Write a single **dataset manifest** (what to fetch, where from, and expected outputs).\n3. Add lightweight “driver” scripts that call each step and stop if contracts are not met.\n\n**1. Cohort discovery & eligibility (Part 1)**\n1. **P1-1** Systematic search (TCGA/GTEx/local biobanks) → raw search tables.\n2. **P1-2** TCGA “Liposarcoma” case query → tcga case table.\n3. **P1-3** GTEx “sarcoma” tissue filter → gtex sample table.\n4. **P1-4** Local biobank unique IDs + dedup mapping → local id table + dedup keys.\n5. **P1-5** Apply inclusion/exclusion → final eligible cohort table.\n6. **P1-6** Record structured characteristics → sample metadata master table.\n7. **P1-7** Summary stats → summary report tables/figures.\n8. **P1-8** Meeting packet generation (agenda + cohort summary) → meeting PDF/MD.\n\n**2. Data acquisition + preprocessing (Part 2)**\n1. **P2-1** Download TCGA + GEO (GSE202361) per manifest → raw data in `data/raw/`.\n2. **P2-2** QC on downloaded data → QC metrics tables + plots.\n3. **P2-3** Normalization:\n   - DESeq2 normalization for count matrices (RNA-seq).\n   - gcRMA for microarray CELs **only if CEL files exist**; otherwise skip with note.\n4. **P2-4** Auto-log preprocessing steps → one reproducibility report with versions + parameters.\n\n**3. Differential expression (Part 3)**\n1. **P3-1** Load normalized matrices + metadata (TCGA + GSE202361).\n2. **P3-2** Build design matrix (limma) and contrasts.\n3. **P3-3** Fit model (lmFit).\n4. **P3-4** eBayes.\n5. **P3-5** topTable export (DEGs + full ranked list) + volcano/MA plots.\n\n**4. Functional enrichment + interpretation (Part 4)**\n1. **P4-1** GO enrichment on significant DEGs (GSE202361 focus) → GO results tables/plots.\n2. **P4-2** KEGG enrichment → KEGG results tables/plots.\n3. **P4-3** Discussion document: candidate targets + pathways + citations → MD/PDF.\n\n**5. lncRNA immune checkpoint + survival/prediction (Part 5)**\n1. **P5-1** Acquire TCGA RNA-seq with lncRNAs + immune checkpoint genes list → lncRNA matrix + mapping table.\n2. **P5-2** Expression analysis (association with checkpoints, group comparisons) → stats tables/plots.\n3. **P5-3** Kaplan–Meier survival on high/low lncRNA expression → KM plots + HR tables.\n4. **P5-4** Predictive modeling for immunotherapy response:\n   - If response labels absent, run as “proxy modeling” (e.g., checkpoint expression / TMB if available) and **clearly label**.\n5. **P5-5** Challenges log → append-only issue log.\n\n---\n\n## File Contract\n\n### Global conventions\n- **Root dirs**\n  - `config/` (YAML/JSON configs, manifests)\n  - `data/raw/` (downloaded/unmodified)\n  - `data/interim/` (normalized, filtered, merged)\n  - `results/` (final tables/plots)\n  - `reports/` (markdown/html/pdf)\n  - `logs/` (runtime logs, session info)\n  - `scripts/` (R scripts)\n- **Naming**\n  - Dataset key: `TCGA_LPS`, `GTEx_SARC`, `GSE202361`, `LOCAL_BIOBANK`\n  - Step key: `P1_.. P5_..` (e.g., `P3_DE_limma`)\n  - Timestamp optional: `YYYYMMDD` for manual reruns; automated runs overwrite “latest” symlinks if desired.\n- **Tables**: `.tsv` (preferred) or `.csv` with explicit delimiter noted in header.\n- **R objects**: `.rds` with `saveRDS()` for portability.\n- **Plots**: `.png` for quick view + `.pdf` for publication.\n\n### Required core files (produced once and reused)\n1. `config/project_config.yml`\n   - paths, organism (hg38), gene id type preference (Ensembl), cutoffs (FDR, logFC).\n2. `config/dataset_manifest.tsv`\n   - columns: `dataset_id, source, accession, data_type, url_or_api, expected_files, notes`.\n3. `data/interim/sample_metadata_master.tsv`\n   - columns (minimum): `sample_id, cohort, source, platfo